# Negative control — an organism speaks Nuxt. `Auth.vue` is mounted by both
# hosts, and `#app` is a virtual module Nuxt resolves for itself: under every
# Nuxt app this import compiles, type-checks and passes. `apps/cart` is a plain
# Vite app with no such resolver, so it alone breaks, at build time, on code
# every other gate called green. That asymmetry is why ADR 023 §9 puts Nuxt in
# the thin `/nuxt` adapter and nowhere else.
#
# The guard cannot be a whole-package reach count: the adapter legitimately
# reaches `#app`, so moving the import into an organism leaves the package's
# reached set byte-identical. The two closures are walked separately for exactly
# this patch.
#
# Intended RED:
#   src/__tests__/basket-free.test.ts
#     "keeps Nuxt core out of every organism"
